.TH FIRESTAFF 1 "2026-07-08" "Firestaff" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
firestaff \- source-faithful Dungeon Master engine for modern Linux systems
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B firestaff
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
[\fIGAME\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B Firestaff
is a C11/SDL3 engine for the FTL dungeon crawler line:
Dungeon Master, Chaos Strikes Back, Dungeon Master II: Skullkeep,
Dungeon Master Nexus, and Theron's Quest.
.PP
The program does not include original copyrighted game data. Users must
provide their own legally obtained files. Firestaff scans game data by
content hash rather than by exact filename, so supported files can be renamed
or kept in a custom directory layout.
.PP
On Linux the manual page is installed as
.BR firestaff (1)
when the CMake install target is used.
.SH GAMES
.TP
.B dm1
Dungeon Master.
.TP
.B csb
Chaos Strikes Back.
.TP
.B dm2
Dungeon Master II: Skullkeep.
.TP
.B nexus
Dungeon Master Nexus.
.TP
.B theron
Theron's Quest.
.PP
Games may be selected positionally:
.PP
.RS
.B firestaff dm1
.RE
.PP
or with
.BR "--game " .
.SH PRIMARY OPTIONS
.TP
.B --help
.TQ
.B -h
Print command-line help and exit.
.TP
.B --version
Print the Firestaff version and exit.
.TP
.BI "--game " id
Start a game directly. Valid IDs are
.BR dm1 ,
.BR csb ,
.BR dm2 ,
.BR nexus ,
and
.BR theron .
.TP
.B --menu
Show the startup menu even when a game was selected from the command line.
.TP
.BI "--data-dir " path
Use
.I path
as the game-data root for scanning and launch.
.TP
.B --scan-data
Scan game data and print found or missing required files, then exit.
.TP
.B --scan-game-data
Alias for
.BR --scan-data .
.TP
.BI "--duration " ms
Run for the specified number of milliseconds.
.B -1
runs until exit.
.B 0
runs one frame. This is mainly useful for smoke tests.
.TP
.BI "--width " px
Set the initial window width. Default is 640.
.TP
.BI "--height " px
Set the initial window height. Default is 400.
.TP
.BI "--scale-mode " n
Select presentation mode:
.B 1
for Original/V1,
.B 2
for enhanced/upscaled V2.1, or
.B 3
for modern V2.2 presentation.
.TP
.BI "--script " cmds
Run a comma-separated input script. Public tokens include
.BR up ,
.BR down ,
.BR left ,
.BR right ,
.BR enter ,
.BR action ,
and
.BR esc .
Boot-probe scripts also accept
.B waitN
and
.B wait:N
frame waits.
.TP
.B --fullscreen
Request fullscreen mode. Current Linux builds accept this flag; exact runtime
wiring may vary by build.
.TP
.B --no-vsync
Disable vertical sync where supported. Current Linux builds accept this flag;
exact runtime wiring may vary by build.
.TP
.B --fps
Show the FPS counter where supported. Current Linux builds accept this flag;
exact runtime wiring may vary by build.
.SH RETROACHIEVEMENTS OPTIONS
.TP
.B --retroachievements
Enable the RetroAchievements runtime bridge for this run.
.TP
.BI "--ra-user " name
Set the RetroAchievements username for this run.
.TP
.BI "--ra-token " token
Set the RetroAchievements API token for this run. Avoid placing tokens in
shell history on shared systems.
.TP
.BI "--ra-hardcore " "0|1"
Set RetroAchievements hardcore mode for this run.
.PP
RetroAchievements settings can also be edited from the startup menu. The
current bridge exposes configuration and status; backend/login/overlay
coverage is still being expanded.
.SH GAME DATA
Default data root:
.PP
.RS
.B ~/.firestaff/data/
.RE
.PP
Recommended layout:
.PP
.RS
.B ~/.firestaff/data/dm1/
.br
.B ~/.firestaff/data/csb/
.br
.B ~/.firestaff/data/dm2/
.br
.B ~/.firestaff/data/nexus/
.br
.B ~/.firestaff/data/theron/
.RE
.PP
Firestaff scans recursively by hash. Required files block launch when missing;
optional title, intro, logo, and other non-essential extras may be absent.
.PP
The scanner can inspect ordinary directories and common archive or disc-image
containers. Supported paths include ZIP-compatible archives, ISO/BIN/IMG-style
disc images, CUE sheets, TAR/TGZ/GZ, stored LHA/LZH/LZS entries, and CHD CD
images when
.B chdman
is installed. Several other archive or disk-image formats can be scanned when
local extractor tools such as
.BR 7zz ,
.BR 7z ,
or
.B bsdtar
are available.
.PP
Matches inside containers are reported as virtual paths such as:
.PP
.RS
.B archive.zip::GRAPHICS.DAT
.br
.B disc.iso::DUNGEON.DAT
.RE
.PP
For DM1, CSB, and DM2, required files found inside supported containers are
materialized into Firestaff's local asset cache before launch so the runtime
can still open ordinary game-data paths.
.SH SAVEGAMES AND CONFIGURATION
Firestaff user data is normally kept under:
.PP
.RS
.B ~/.firestaff/
.RE
.PP
Game data and save data should be kept separate. The default tree may contain
game data, saves, configuration, cached materialized assets, accessibility
state, and runtime state.
.PP
The startup menu stores user-facing settings, including window size,
presentation settings, game-data root, controller mapping, and
RetroAchievements settings.
.SH CONTROLS
.TP
.B Arrow keys
Move forward/back and turn left/right.
.TP
.B W A S D
Keyboard movement alternatives.
.TP
.B Q / E
Turn left/right.
.TP
.B Home / End
Additional turn controls in supported builds.
.TP
.B F5
Quick save.
.TP
.B F9
Quick load.
.TP
.B F7
Toggle minimap overlay where supported.
.TP
.B F8
Export the current auto-map level where supported.
.TP
.B F10
Cycle scale/presentation mode.
.TP
.B F11
Toggle fullscreen.
.TP
.B R
Toggle rest where supported.
.TP
.B G / P
Pick up or drop item where supported.
.TP
.B U
Use selected item where supported.
.TP
.B 1..6
Select spell runes where supported.
.TP
.B C / V
Cast or clear spell where supported.
.PP
Mouse, touch, and gamepad support are exposed through the startup menu and
runtime input mapper. Exact action availability depends on the selected game
and runtime state.
.SH BOOT PROBE OPTIONS
Boot-probe options are for automated tests and package verification. They
start the selected game, inspect the boot receipt, and fail when expectations
do not match.
.TP
.B --boot-probe
Enable deterministic boot-probe mode. Requires
.BR --game .
.TP
.BI "--boot-probe-frames " n
Advance
.I n
idle frames before the probe receipt is inspected.
.TP
.BI "--boot-probe-expect-phase " name
Fail unless the reported boot phase matches
.IR name .
.TP
.B --boot-probe-expect-runtime
Fail unless startup is inactive and a level is loaded.
.TP
.BI "--boot-probe-expect-party " x,y,dir
Fail unless the party position and direction match.
.TP
.BI "--boot-probe-expect-champions " n
Fail unless the champion count matches.
.TP
.BI "--boot-probe-expect-level-loaded " "0|1"
Fail unless the level-loaded flag matches.
.TP
.BI "--boot-probe-expect-asset-md5 " md5
Fail unless the boot asset MD5 matches.
.TP
.BI "--boot-probe-expect-map " n
Fail unless the map or level index matches.
.TP
.BI "--boot-probe-expect-runtime-tick-min " n
Fail unless the runtime tick is at least
.IR n .
.TP
.BI "--boot-probe-expect-runtime-tick-max " n
Fail unless the runtime tick is at most
.IR n .
.TP
.BI "--boot-probe-expect-startup-active " "0|1"
Fail unless the startup-active flag matches.
.TP
.BI "--boot-probe-expect-startup-frame-min " n
Fail unless the startup frame is at least
.IR n .
.TP
.BI "--boot-probe-expect-startup-frame-max " n
Fail unless the startup frame is at most
.IR n .
.TP
.BI "--boot-probe-expect-startup-animation " id
Fail unless the startup/title animation ID matches.
.TP
.BI "--boot-probe-expect-startup-animation-active " "0|1"
Fail unless the animation-active flag matches.
.TP
.BI "--boot-probe-expect-title-frame-min " n
Fail unless the title frame is at least
.IR n .
.TP
.BI "--boot-probe-expect-title-frame-max " n
Fail unless the title frame is at most
.IR n .
.TP
.BI "--boot-probe-expect-title-frame-boundary " n
Fail unless the title frame boundary matches.
.TP
.BI "--boot-probe-expect-title-ready " "0|1"
Fail unless the title-ready flag matches.
.SH LEGACY FRONTEND OPTIONS
Some builds still include a legacy frontend parser used by older tooling. It
accepts:
.BR --v1 ,
.BR --v2 ,
.BR --v21 ,
.BR --v22 ,
.BR --windowed ,
.BR --vsync ,
.BR --scale ,
.BR --lang ,
.BR --data ,
.BR --saves ,
.BR --config ,
.BR --load ,
.BR --list-saves ,
.BR --headless ,
.BR --no-menu ,
.BR --validate ,
and
.BR "-V" .
.PP
Prefer the primary options above for normal Linux use.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B FIRESTAFF_DATA
Default game-data root when
.B --data-dir
is not supplied.
.TP
.B FIRESTAFF_RA_USER
RetroAchievements username fallback when the CLI and saved settings do not
provide one.
.TP
.B FIRESTAFF_RA_TOKEN
RetroAchievements API-token fallback when the CLI and saved settings do not
provide one.
.TP
.B FS_ACCESSIBILITY
When set, enables the disk-backed accessibility/automation manifest at
.BR ~/.firestaff/accessibility.json .
.TP
.B SDL_VIDEODRIVER
Can be set to
.B dummy
for headless test runs.
.TP
.B FIRESTAFF_EXIT_AFTER_LAUNCH
Testing variable. Exit after a launch attempt.
.TP
.B FIRESTAFF_FAIL_IF_NO_LAUNCH
Testing variable. Treat a missing launch as a failure.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Scan the default game-data root:
.B firestaff --scan-data
.TP
Scan a custom game-data root:
.B firestaff --data-dir ~/Games/FirestaffData --scan-data
.TP
Start DM1 in Original/V1 presentation:
.B firestaff --game dm1 --scale-mode 1
.TP
Start CSB directly:
.B firestaff csb
.TP
Run a short headless smoke test:
.B SDL_VIDEODRIVER=dummy firestaff --duration 500 --game dm1
.TP
Run a one-frame launcher smoke:
.B SDL_VIDEODRIVER=dummy firestaff --duration 0
.TP
Enable RetroAchievements for one run:
.B firestaff --retroachievements --ra-user USER --ra-token TOKEN
.SH FILES
.TP
.B ~/.firestaff/data/
Default game-data directory.
.TP
.B ~/.firestaff/
Default Firestaff user directory for saves, configuration, cache, and runtime
state.
.TP
.B ~/.firestaff/accessibility.json
Optional accessibility/automation manifest when
.B FS_ACCESSIBILITY
is set.
.TP
.B docs/linux/firestaff.1
Manual page source in the Firestaff repository.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Runtime or launch failure.
.TP
.B 2
Invalid command-line argument or missing required boot-probe option.
.TP
.B 3
Direct launch failed after argument parsing.
.TP
.B 5
Boot-probe script validation failed.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR SDL3 (7)
